C:\\Users\\foste\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-08-30\\wh\\outputs\\MODEL_LIBRARY_BOOTSTRAP_2026-08-31.md\n+# Model Library Bootstrap\n+\n+Date: 2026-08-31  \n+Purpose: build a durable, portable open-model library for the RIB, local dogfood, and later read-only sharing.\n+\n+## Operating rule\n+\n+Do not treat a downloaded checkpoint as a useful model until it has a passport and one receipt-backed probe. The library stores:\n+\n+```text\n+model identity + upstream revision + license\n+weights/tokenizer/config hashes\n+runtime and quantization\n+hardware envelope\n+capability and refusal/authority probes\n+cost, latency, context, and failure receipts\n+```\n+\n+The passport is the map. The weights are territory. A model may be indexed remotely before it is downloaded locally.\n+\n+## Storage doctrine\n+\n+- Keep the RIB, manifests, golden probe set, receipts, and irreplaceable research local first.\n+- Keep one canonical tested quantization per family locally; record other quantizations as pointers until demand or hardware justifies them.\n+- Never count raw capacity as usable capacity. With one parity disk, a 30 TB raw pool has materially less data capacity.\n+- Use SnapRAID/mergerfs or an equivalent content-addressed pool, with SMART checks and a restore drill.\n+- Models are replaceable; primary books, art, notes, and research may not be. Give those a second copy and a separate license/provenance record.\n+- Share through a read-only authenticated service over the private network. Do not expose a write-capable model directory or credentials to model-facing tools.\n+\n+## Suggested shared layout\n+\n+```text\n+library/\n+  models/<family>/<revision>/\n+    manifest.json\n+    weights/<one-tested-quantization>/\n+    tokenizer/\n+    runtime/\n+    probes/\n+    receipts/\n+  corpora/<name>/<revision>/manifest.json\n+  books/<name>/manifest.json\n+  art/<name>/manifest.json\n+  indexes/model-atlas.jsonl\n+  indexes/content-digests.jsonl\n+```\n+\n+Books and art enter the corpus only when we own them, they are public domain, or their license permits the intended use and sharing. For restricted material, keep a metadata passport and local rights record rather than redistributing the bytes.\n+\n+## Passport schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"model_id\": \"org/name\",\n+  \"upstream_revision\": \"commit-or-release\",\n+  \"source_url\": \"official-model-card-url\",\n+  \"license\": \"exact-license-name-and-url\",\n+  \"architecture\": \"dense|moe|multimodal|audio|embedding\",\n+  \"parameters\": {\"total\": 0, \"active\": 0},\n+  \"modalities\": [\"text\"],\n+  \"context_tokens\": 0,\n+  \"files\": [{\"path\": \"...\", \"bytes\": 0, \"sha256\": \"sha256:...\"}],\n+  \"quantization\": {\"format\": \"GGUF|safetensors|...\", \"bits\": 0},\n+  \"runtime\": [\"llama.cpp\", \"vllm\", \"transformers\"],\n+  \"hardware\": {\"min_vram_gb\": 0, \"min_ram_gb\": 0},\n+  \"tool_contract\": {\"supports_tools\": false, \"schema\": \"...\"},\n+  \"probes\": [{\"pack\": \"riddler-v1\", \"receipt\": \"...\", \"score\": 0}],\n+  \"economics\": {\"download_gb\": 0, \"run_cost_class\": \"local|burst|remote\"},\n+  \"status\": \"indexed|downloaded|probed|promoted|quarantined\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## First local set\n+\n+Choose one representative per tier. Do not fetch every size or every community quantization on day one.\n+\n+1. **Micro router / cheap worker:** Gemma 3 270M or 1B. Use for classification, compression, routing, and pressure preflight. Google describes Gemma 3 as open-weight and multimodal, with 128K context and multiple sizes; access requires accepting its usage license.\n+2. **Compact generalist:** Qwen3-4B. Use for cheap local synthesis, board triage, and bounded worker jobs. Keep the upstream revision and model card beside the quantization.\n+3. **Compact reasoning/code baseline:** Phi-4. The official card identifies a 14B text model under MIT with a 16K context window; it is a useful explicit-license comparison point, not a universal winner.\n+4. **Local multimodal:** Gemma 3 4B or 12B, selected only after the image probe and VRAM test. Keep it separate from the text-only routing lane.\n+5. **Code specialist:** Devstral-Small-2-24B-Instruct, or the smallest current Mistral code model that passes the local tool-contract probe. The official Mistral collection lists Devstral-Small-2-24B-Instruct-2512 and larger Devstral variants.\n+6. **Reasoning reference:** DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-14B or 32B. Store one quantization only after a timed local/burst test; reasoning models are expensive in latency and context even when the weights are available.\n+\n+## Watchlist, not automatic downloads\n+\n+Track newer Qwen, Mistral, Gemma, Llama, and small-specialist releases in the atlas first. Promote only when the passport has an exact revision, license, reproducible download, runtime compatibility, and a probe receipt. “Uncensored” or “abliterated” is a behavior label, not a quality or provenance guarantee; quarantine such weights until their source and behavior are recorded.\n+\n+## The first dogfood run\n+\n+```text\n+1. Pick the smallest two models that fit the current machine.\n+2. Download from the official model page at a pinned revision.\n+3. Hash weights, tokenizer, config, and license.\n+4. Run one fixed probe pack: summarize, classify, extract, code, refuse/authority, and tool schema.\n+5. Record tokens/sec, peak memory, latency, output variance, and failure class.\n+6. Serve them read-only through the shared model directory.\n+7. Let the atlas predict a route; compare prediction with the receipt.\n+8. Promote only the model whose receipt earns the slot.\n+```\n+\n+## What 30 TB buys us\n+\n+It buys local continuity, reproducible checkpoints, a research corpus, and independence from a single provider. It does not automatically buy useful intelligence. The high-value asset is the compact invariant library: passports, probe packs, receipts, adapters, and RIB pointers. Those let a remote model or a future local model re-enter the same experiment without rereading the entire archive.\n+\n+## Falsifiers\n+\n+- A model passport routes correctly only because the operator already knew the answer.\n+- The same pinned model and probe produce materially different results with no recorded environmental change.\n+- A downloaded weight has no exact revision, hash, license, or restore path.\n+- A shared server can mutate the library or expose secrets through the model-facing interface.\n+- The 30 TB pool cannot restore one known model and one known research artifact from its manifests.\n+\n+## Starting point\n+\n+Start with the current machine's actual VRAM/RAM report, not the desired hardware. Build the two-model probe receipt first. Expand storage only after the receipt tells us whether the bottleneck is weights, corpus, bandwidth, GPU memory, or retrieval.\n+\n+### Official starting references\n+\n+- Google Gemma 3 model card: https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-3-4b-pt\n+- Qwen3-4B model card: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-4B\n+- Microsoft Phi-4 model card: https://huggingface.co/microsoft/phi-4\n+- Mistral official model collection: https://huggingface.co/mistralai/collections\n+- DeepSeek-R1 official model card: https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1\n*** End Patch";
