C:\\Users\\foste\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-08-30\\wh\\outputs\\MODEL_LIBRARY_BOOTSTRAP_2026-08-31.md\n@@\n ## Watchlist, not automatic downloads\n \n Track newer Qwen, Mistral, Gemma, Llama, and small-specialist releases in the atlas first. Promote only when the passport has an exact revision, license, reproducible download, runtime compatibility, and a probe receipt. “Uncensored” or “abliterated” is a behavior label, not a quality or provenance guarantee; quarantine such weights until their source and behavior are recorded.\n+\n+## Useful abliterated shelf\n+\n+These are candidates for controlled red-team, creative, and refusal-behavior experiments—not default OpenClaw workers and not public endpoints.\n+\n+- `huihui-ai/Huihui-Qwen3.8-27B-abliterated-GGUF`: Apache-2.0 on the model card; the listed 4-bit variants are about 14.4–17.4 GB, 8-bit variants about 29–31.5 GB, and BF16 about 54.7 GB. The maintainer describes the transformation as a crude proof of concept and warns that safety filtering is reduced.\n+- `0bserverx/Qwen3.8-27B-Heretic-Abliterated-Uncensored-GGUF`: Apache-2.0 is stated for the repository and retained base model; its recommended 4-bit Q4_K_M file is about 16.55 GB. The card notes extra memory for optional MTP/vision pieces and recommends controlled research use.\n+- `culturerevolt/gemma-4-12b-heretic-abliterated-GGUF`: Apache-2.0 on the card; 4-bit files are about 6.64–7.38 GB. This is the practical small abliterated candidate for a constrained machine.\n+- `mlabonne/Qwen3-30B-A3B-abliterated`: index it, but do not promote it yet; its own card says it is work-in-progress and not recommended at the moment.\n+\n+Put these under `models/quarantine/`, give them no credentials, shell, network mutation, or effect-broker grant, and require a fixed probe receipt before promotion. A refusal change is not a capability grant. The useful comparison is: same task, same envelope, base model versus abliterated model, with helpfulness, factuality, variance, tool obedience, and refusal behavior recorded separately.\n+\n+## Capacity estimate\n+\n+Approximate model-file sizes at 4-bit, before runtime cache and metadata:\n+\n+```text\n+12B  ≈ 7 GB       27–30B  ≈ 15–18 GB       70B  ≈ 35–45 GB\n+120B ≈ 65–75 GB   400B+   ≈ hundreds of GB   1T   ≈ half a TB or more\n+```\n+\n+Therefore 30 TB raw can hold roughly 1,500–1,900 27B Q4 files or 600–850 70B Q4 files in pure arithmetic. A one-parity pool with only about 20–24 TB usable capacity lowers those counts, and keeping two or three quantizations multiplies consumption. The sensible target is one tested quantization per family plus a small quarantine shelf; reserve the rest for research, receipts, indexes, and restore copies.\n*** End Patch";
