C:\\Users\\foste\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-08-30\\wh\\outputs\\MODEL_LIBRARY_BOOTSTRAP_2026-08-31.md\n@@\n ## What 30 TB buys us\n \n It buys local continuity, reproducible checkpoints, a research corpus, and independence from a single provider. It does not automatically buy useful intelligence. The high-value asset is the compact invariant library: passports, probe packs, receipts, adapters, and RIB pointers. Those let a remote model or a future local model re-enter the same experiment without rereading the entire archive.\n+\n+## Known recurring fleet: local weights versus behavior mining\n+\n+From the models named in this operation, the honest split is:\n+\n+| Model/family | Local weight status | What belongs in the library |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| GLM-5.3-Flash | Downloadable; MIT on the official card; 321B total / 18B active; local serving frameworks are listed | One pinned weight archive if storage allows, but route it to burst/distributed serving rather than the desktop by default |\n+| DeepSeek-V4-Flash | Official open-weight release; 284B total / 13B active; 1M context; FP4+FP8 mixed release | One pinned archive plus a remote-serving receipt; active parameters do not mean only 13B weights need to be stored |\n+| Grok 4.6 | Provider-facing model; official docs expose API/tool use and pricing, not downloadable weights | Model passport, prompt/probe corpus, output envelopes, cost/latency, tool behavior, and disagreement signatures |\n+| GPT-5.3 / ChatGPT lane | Provider-facing API model; official page exposes API snapshots and endpoints, not downloadable weights | Same behavioral atlas; pin snapshot IDs where available and record provider responses |\n+| Z.ai/DeepSeek/Groq/NVIDIA lanes generally | Some have open checkpoints, some are API or inference-provider routes | Verify each exact model ID and revision; never infer downloadable weights from a provider name |\n+\n+The official GLM card says the model can be served with vLLM, SGLang, Transformers, KTransformers, or Unsloth, but its parameter count makes it a serious multi-device or remote target. DeepSeek’s official release likewise distinguishes total from activated parameters: the router can activate 13B per token while the archive still contains the full 284B expert system. [GLM-5.3-Flash](https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash) · [DeepSeek-V4-Flash](https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash) · [Grok 4.6 docs](https://docs.x.ai/developers/models/grok-4.6) · [GPT-5.3 API model](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.3-chat-latest)\n+\n+For provider-only models, “local mining” means replayable behavioral mining:\n+\n+```text\n+fixed probe -> provider call -> raw response envelope\n+           -> normalized claims/disagreements/tool behavior\n+           -> hash + model snapshot + cost/latency receipt\n+           -> local atlas and cheap-agent synthesis\n+```\n+\n+This preserves much of the useful fleet knowledge without claiming to possess proprietary weights. It also makes provider replacement possible: a local or open model can be tested against the same probe set and compared on behavior rather than brand.\n*** End Patch";
